BEGIN_TEXT
Your card is your station's public half: its call and fingerprint. Give
it freely. The fingerprint, read aloud or checked in person, is how
another station knows the card is really yours.

A keymaster issues key tapes. You choose whose tapes you take: check
their fingerprint by voice or in person, then accept them. No bundle,
handout or message can name a keymaster for you.

A key tape is sealed to your card, so only your box can open it. A long
tape comes over the air in numbered parts; the box holds them until every
part is here. Missing parts are asked for by number (PARTS_ASK).
END
